%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat may be so, but it's also not exactly the epitome of\npoliteness to point it out to people.\d%K%P
「也许本应该那样的，\n但我觉得这话从你嘴里说出来，那就变成强迫了」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dI see you still haven't learned when to keep your\nwitticisms to yourself. You're the one who always ends up\nregretting them later.\d%K%P
「你还是那么多话啊。\n明明总是之后就后悔的」%K%P
It was common sense to mind one's manners around every\nmember of society. But it was also quite crude to force\nmanners upon others, even if they were slightly out of\nline.%K%P
讲礼貌是社会人士的常识。\n但是，作为社会人士强迫他人讲礼貌就有点过分了。%K%P
The adult world subsisted on such oddly contradictory\nnotions.%K%P
大人的世界，总是像这样，\n有着些许的矛盾之处。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThe proverb \dregret always comes too late\d makes little\nsense to me. I mean, if it didn't come too late, you would\nhave nothing to regret to begin with, don't you think?\d%K%P
「『事后后悔莫及』，我觉得这句俗语没有造好。\n“只有事后才能后悔，所以事前怎么可能会后悔”\n从词语搭配的角度加常用语境来解释明显是这样的」%K%P
Then again, it was just how -we- communicated.%K%P
嘛， 那个暂且不提，唯独让人讨厌的话是没法忘掉的。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dLet's begin.\d%K%P
「开始吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOf course.\d%K%P
「请多关照」%K%P
...It took us almost half a year to return to that level\nof mutual comfort, though.%K%P
…我们的对话都能深入到这种程度了。\n虽说是花了半年的时间。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dOkay, let's start from the results of Mitoko's mock\nexaminations.\d%K%P
「好了，首先从美都子\n上个月模拟考试的结果开始说吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dShe scored 455 points across five subjects, which makes\nher the second best of the school year and the top of her\nclass! She got a perfect score at Japanese! ...Only 78 at\nMath, though, which you teach.\d%K%P
「五门课程总共４５５分。\n综合成绩年级排名第二。班级里面当然是第一。\n而且国语居然是满分！…不过麻实教的数学是７８分」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...You have a good memory, I see.\d%K%P
「…你记得还真清楚啊」%K%P
